WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.016
How do you pick the right attention mechanism for a
long-range Transformer task,

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:08.074
and could mixing several types work even better?

00:00:08.154 --> 00:00:09.539
This paper, DARTFormer,

00:00:09.619 --> 00:00:14.253
adapts differentiable neural architecture search to
answer both questions.

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:19.986
The authors build a supernetwork that contains many
efficient attention types in parallel,

00:00:20.066 --> 00:00:23.999
then use a masked validation accuracy drop metric
to rank them.

00:00:24.079 --> 00:00:28.140
Their search reliably finds the best single
attention for a task,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.682
but a surprising second result emerges:
heterogeneous Transformers that combine several

00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:36.930
attention types beat the average homogeneous model,

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.160
yet never beat the single best one.
